Body:
Tracked this down to a one-line fix. The root cause is in `packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui/routes/session/index.tsx`
The <markdown> element is passed `internalBlockMode="top-level"`, which in Markdown.ts (@opentui/core) causes resolveTableStyle() to default to "columns":

```js
// opentui Markdown.ts
private resolveTableStyle(...) {
  ...
  return this._internalBlockMode === "top-level" ? "columns" : "grid"
}
// resolveTableRenderableOptions()
const borders = this._tableOptions?.borders ?? style === "grid"  // -> false
```

"columns" style disables borders by default. Passing `tableOptions={{ style: "grid" }}` explicitly fixes it:

```diff
 <markdown
   syntaxStyle={syntax()}
   streaming={true}
   internalBlockMode="top-level"
+  tableOptions={{ style: "grid" }}
   content={props.part.text.trim()}
   conceal={ctx.conceal()}
   fg={theme.markdownText}
   bg={theme.background}
 />
```

