This should be reopened because the underlying issue is still present on current `dev`: provider-thrown `ContextOverflowError` still forces `ctx.needsCompaction = true` even when `compaction.auto === false`.

The existing `compaction.auto` guard only covers proactive token-threshold overflow checks, not the provider-error path fixed by #17936. As a result, users can still get forced into automatic compaction despite explicitly disabling it.
